{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>If there arise in your midst a prophet.</b> The verse's saying <b>prophet</b> means — even if he is established as a prophet, even if he would be trusted by you if he told you to transgress a certain commandment temporarily, like Elijah on Mount Carmel (I Kings 18), and so forth — nevertheless, if he tells you to worship idolatry, he is liable to the death penalty." "<b>And he gives you a sign, etc.</b> One must know why Scripture did not mention at the outset the prophet's statement — the matter concerning which he gave the sign, etc. Further, one must know the intent of the verse's saying <b>and the sign comes, etc.</b> <b>saying, etc.</b> — is the sign the one speaking? Is it not the prophet who speaks to worship idolatry, for which he becomes liable to the death penalty?" "<b>And it appears</b> that Scripture intends to address a prophet who comes and speaks in this manner: HaShem said to him that if he performs this miracle or this sign, the intent of the sign is to say that we should worship idolatry. And if the sign and the miracle come about in this manner, the intent is not so — on the contrary, it is to abhor it and burn it according to its first judgment. <b>And the sign and the miracle come</b> — meaning, even though he said only either this or that, and both of them came, the sign and the miracle, and they were in the order that he said they would declare the intent of HaShem that His will is that they worship idolatry — <b>do not listen, etc.</b>, and the prophet is liable to the death penalty, etc. — even though he did not state definitively in his words that they should worship until the coming of the sign and the miracle, and they are the ones that speak to worship, and further, that he said only either a sign or a miracle and both of them came — even so, do not listen, etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:16:59.616114621Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}